            "text": "{\n  \"primary_meaning\": \"The character, authority, essence, and identity of the person to whom it belongs. In biblical symbolism, particularly regarding God or Jesus, a name is not merely a label but represents the totality of the person's revealed nature and sovereign power.\",\n  \"primary_basis\": [\n    \"Exodus 3:13-15\",\n    \"Exodus 34:5-7\",\n    \"Proverbs 22:1\",\n    \"John 14:13-14\",\n    \"Acts 4:12\",\n    \"Philippians 2:9-11\"\n  ],\n  \"alternatives\": [\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"Ownership, protection, and covenantal belonging (e.g., having a name placed or written upon someone)\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Numbers 6:27\",\n        \"Revelation 3:12\",\n        \"Revelation 14:1\",\n        \"Revelation 22:4\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"common\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"Reputation, legacy, or enduring memory after death\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Proverbs 10:7\",\n        \"Ecclesiastes 7:1\",\n        \"Isaiah 56:5\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"common\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"A localized, tangible manifestation of God's presence, often associated with the Temple (Deuteronomistic 'Name Theology')\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Deuteronomy 12:5\",\n        \"Deuteronomy 12:11\",\n        \"1 Kings 8:29\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"minority\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"meaning\": \"A formulaic source of independent spiritual power or incantation\",\n      \"basis\": [\n        \"Acts 19:13-15\"\n      ],\n      \"prominence\": \"rare\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"has_settled_consensus\": true,\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"There is wide consensus in biblical scholarship that 'name' (shem in Hebrew, onoma in Greek) carries profound ontological weight. To pray or act 'in the name of' Jesus is universally understood in orthodox Christian teaching as acting by His delegated authority and in alignment with His character, rather than merely reciting a formula.\"\n}",
